# The GOOD half of finding PA-08-F8 of bd inc-tek.8.8: the Staff of the Abyss
# says it is "an inert stick in the hands of any good character", so a good
# fifth-level caster must get nothing from it. Read by
# tools/check_staff_abyss_alignment.sh.
#
# WHY THIS FILE REPEATS tools/keys/chargen-mage.keys INSTEAD OF INCLUDING IT.
# That file answers the alignment prompt with the literal letter 'e', which is
# Neutral. Nothing in wizard mode can change a character's alignment after
# generation -- the menu (src/Debug.cpp:534-572) has no such option -- so the
# good character has to be made good at the prompt, and the prompt is in the
# middle of the file. Everything AFTER generation is shared, and lives in
# tools/keys/staff-abyss-alignment-body.keys.
#
# The character is otherwise the same orc mage the non-good half uses: same
# race, same class, same specialty, same seed. Only the alignment differs, so
# only the alignment can explain a difference in the result.

a       # Initial Choices: [a] Create a New Character
n       # Alter the character generation options? -- no
y       # Your options will place the game in Explore Mode. Continue? -- yes
i       # Race:     [i] Orc
a       # Subrace:  [a] Orc (Standard)
d       # Class:    [d] Mage
a       # Attributes: the first of the five offered sets

@choose "Neutral Good"
        #   By name, not by letter. FindMenuEntry ranks an exact match above
        #   an overlap (src/Wposix.cpp:984-997), so this cannot be captured by
        #   the plain "Neutral" entry sitting in the same list.

e       # Wizard specialty: [e] Evocation
a       # First feat
a       # Second feat

# Skill Manager. RIGHT spends a rank on the selected skill and stops at the
# skill's maximum, DOWN moves to the next skill, so three RIGHTs per skill
# spends everything available without needing to know how many ranks this
# character has. Character generation will not let go until the pool is empty.
RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN
RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN
ENTER y # Done, and confirm keeping the ranks

y       # Do you wish to worship <god>? -- yes
a       # Personality archetype
a a a   # Three starting spells

@include staff-abyss-alignment-body.keys
